    "result_text": "All **42 tests pass** \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS. The implementation is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional, city-validated `postcode` on owner creation (`POST /api/owners`), following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**Contract / DTO** \u2014 Added `postcode` to the `OwnerFields` schema in `openapi.yml` (`type: string`, `pattern: \"^[0-9]{4}$\"`, optional). This regenerates both `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and `OwnerDto` (response), and the `^[0-9]{4}$` pattern makes a malformed postcode a **400** via existing bean validation (`@Valid` in `ValidateOwnerFields`).\n\n**Persistence** \u2014 Added a `postcode` field/column to the `Owner` entity and to every DB schema (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`). MapStruct maps `postcode` automatically by name in both directions, so it's stored on create and returned on GET. Also fixed the positional seed inserts in `hsqldb/data.sql` (added the extra `NULL`) that the new column shifted.\n\n**Range validation** \u2014 New step `ValidatePostcode` wired into the POST pipeline right after `validate`:\n- Absent/blank postcode \u2192 accepted unchanged (backward-compatible).\n- City with a known region (via the existing `Locality` helper) \u2192 the 4 digits must fall in NSW 2000\u20132099 / VIC 3000\u20133099 / QLD 4000\u20134099, else it throws.\n- City with no known region \u2192 any 4-digit postcode accepted.\n\n**Error handling** \u2014 New checked `InvalidPostcodeException`, its `InvalidPostcodeHandler` (returns **400** with `postcode` in the `errors` array, mirroring the telephone/field handlers), and the escalation YAML wiring them together.\n\nThe three new Cp29 tests (valid postcode stored & returned, owner without postcode still accepted, malformed postcode rejected 400) pass, and all 39 pre-existing tests remain green.",
